<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Forterre et al. (2005) Nature Doubly-Curved Shallow Shell Elastic Energy & Saddle-Node Cusp Catastrophe in Dionaea muscipula, coupled to a P1-FEM trigger-hair action potential and Ca2+ counting gate (Dionaea muscipula (Venus flytrap bilobed leaf trap))",
        "Forterre et al. (2005) Nature Doubly-Curved Shallow Shell Elastic Energy & Saddle-Node Cusp Catastrophe in Dionaea muscipula, coupled to a P1-FEM trigger-hair action potential and Ca2+ counting gate faithfully reproduces Dionaea muscipula (Venus flytrap bilobed leaf trap) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Dionaea muscipula (Venus flytrap bilobed leaf trap) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 80.4/100, audit 2026-10-19-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/de27b685/2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py> ;
    schema:about "Dionaea muscipula (Venus flytrap bilobed leaf trap)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Hodgkin-Huxley-type Ca2+/Cl-/K+ channel kinetics, a trigger-hair lever/podium FEM, mechanical feedback from shell curvature onto the electrics, digitised Forterre (2005) Fig. 2-3 time series, or online-verified DOIs for the 8 electrophysiology references added in Pass 3",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D doubly-curved shallow shell energy U(kappa_x, kappa_y) with Gauss stretching penalty, L-BFGS-B equilibrium relaxation, cusp fold metrics and RK45 inertial + poroelastic snap dynamics across alpha in [0.2, 5.0] (Pass 2)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Boltzmann trigger-hair open probability -> receptor potential clamp on hair-footprint nodes -> P1-FEM IMEX FitzHugh-Nagumo action potential on a flat Delaunay lobe planform (2057 nodes), validated against the exact Nagumo front speed; per-node Ca2+ integrator with two-touch counting; lumped activated-area fraction A(t) gating the active rest curvature of the shell solver (Pass 3)",
        "reported_in_source: Forterre et al. (2005): the Dionaea lobe is a doubly-curved shallow shell whose stretching-bending coupling alpha = L^4 kappa^2/h^2 produces a bistable snap-through (cusp catastrophe) once alpha exceeds a threshold; closure takes ~100 ms, far faster than the poroelastic limit; curvature-relief strip cutting abolishes snapping",
        "reported_in_source: Hedrich & Neher (2018), Böhm et al. (2016), Suda et al. (2020): two trigger-hair touches within ~30 s (two action potentials, a Ca2+ threshold) are required to close the trap; Hodick & Sievers (1988) / Volkov et al. (2008): the lobe AP propagates at cm/s speeds with ~1-2 s duration (values conflict between sources)",
        "reported_in_source: Scherzer et al. (2019), Procko et al. (2021): trigger hairs are micronewton mechanosensors with the stretch-activated channel FLYC1",
        "transfer_boundary: AP_DIFFUSIVITY_CM2_S, AP_TAU_V_S, TRIGGER_HAIR_F_HALF_UN, CA_INCREMENT_PER_AP and CA_DECAY_TAU_S are model constants chosen so that the analytic speed, threshold and memory window land in the recalled literature ranges; agreement in measurements 14 and 17 is therefore parameter-driven, only the FEM-load elevation above the 0-D threshold (liminal ratio 1.55) is emergent",
        "transfer_boundary: The `*_obs` columns of venus_flytrap_snap_buckling_reference.json are generated by the same model, so measurements 3-6 (r = 1.0000) are self-consistency checks, not comparisons with Forterre et al. (2005) data",
        "transfer_boundary: The electrical problem is solved on a FLAT 2D planform mesh, not on the curved mid-surface, and the FEM does not see kappa(t); the motor response is a scalar gate A(t) on a two-mode shell, not a spatially resolved turgor field" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "7. Elastic Shell/Sheet Buckling" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Gyri, Villi, Loops & Snap-Shells" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Wrinkling lambda ~ h(E_f/E_s)^1/3" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Dionaea" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/de27b685/2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py; output: docs/media/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling_comparison.png; organism: Dionaea muscipula (Venus flytrap bilobed leaf trap); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/de27b685; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 58961469a41c2bee9701d676c847ef1e7a9835ee5baa9146d199bf480fec0179; artifact_sha256: 435ac24cf8de9544178ac2abf5bf4f73f1d294d040244b2c5553a08c90ccd973; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/dionaea_muscipula_trap_lobe_specimen.jpg=f2738290d66e4418..., datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/paper_citations.bib=b7c452b03e1fbba6..., datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/scout_manifest.json=572531a0986c798e..., datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/trigger_hair_ap_reference.json=76a6cb4ec8536b9a..., datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling_reference.json=593d9449e870fcf2...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Forterre et al. (2005): the Dionaea lobe is a doubly-curved shallow shell whose stretching-bending coupling alpha = L^4 kappa^2/h^2 produces a bistable snap-through (cusp catastrophe) once alpha exceeds a threshold; closure takes ~100 ms, far faster than the poroelastic limit; curvature-relief strip cutting abolishes snapping | Hedrich & Neher (2018), Böhm et al. (2016), Suda et al. (2020): two trigger-hair touches within ~30 s (two action potentials, a Ca2+ threshold) are required to close the trap; Hodick & Sievers (1988) / Volkov et al. (2008): the lobe AP propagates at cm/s speeds with ~1-2 s duration (values conflict between sources) | Scherzer et al. (2019), Procko et al. (2021): trigger hairs are micronewton mechanosensors with the stretch-activated channel FLYC1; reconstructed_in_script: 2D doubly-curved shallow shell energy U(kappa_x, kappa_y) with Gauss stretching penalty, L-BFGS-B equilibrium relaxation, cusp fold metrics and RK45 inertial + poroelastic snap dynamics across alpha in [0.2, 5.0] (Pass 2) | Boltzmann trigger-hair open probability -> receptor potential clamp on hair-footprint nodes -> P1-FEM IMEX FitzHugh-Nagumo action potential on a flat Delaunay lobe planform (2057 nodes), validated against the exact Nagumo front speed; per-node Ca2+ integrator with two-touch counting; lumped activated-area fraction A(t) gating the active rest curvature of the shell solver (Pass 3); transfer_boundary: The electrical problem is solved on a FLAT 2D planform mesh, not on the curved mid-surface, and the FEM does not see kappa(t); the motor response is a scalar gate A(t) on a two-mode shell, not a spatially resolved turgor field | AP_DIFFUSIVITY_CM2_S, AP_TAU_V_S, TRIGGER_HAIR_F_HALF_UN, CA_INCREMENT_PER_AP and CA_DECAY_TAU_S are model constants chosen so that the analytic speed, threshold and memory window land in the recalled literature ranges; agreement in measurements 14 and 17 is therefore parameter-driven, only the FEM-load elevation above the 0-D threshold (liminal ratio 1.55) is emergent | The `*_obs` columns of venus_flytrap_snap_buckling_reference.json are generated by the same model, so measurements 3-6 (r = 1.0000) are self-consistency checks, not comparisons with Forterre et al. (2005) data; does_not_claim: Hodgkin-Huxley-type Ca2+/Cl-/K+ channel kinetics, a trigger-hair lever/podium FEM, mechanical feedback from shell curvature onto the electrics, digitised Forterre (2005) Fig. 2-3 time series, or online-verified DOIs for the 8 electrophysiology references added in Pass 3]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00394867>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0001-8708(70)90023-X>,
