<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Forterre et al. (2005) Nature Doubly-Curved Shallow Shell Elastic Energy & Saddle-Node Cusp Catastrophe in Dionaea muscipula, coupled to a P1-FEM trigger-hair action potential and Ca2+ counting gate — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module header maps Laws 1-5 to the Lean theorems and to the paper equations (L24-93), Section 3b constants are each commented `model` or `approx.` (L683-700), and `morphoeval/math_kg_loops/forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.yaml` registers all 5 equations with `lean_locus` and single-range `code_locus` refreshed to current line numbers. Deductions: Panel A shape factors (L1187-1214), the hard-coded 56.0 ms in `speedup_ratio_over_poroelastic` (L214) and the 0.21-0.30 s Stage II shading (L1317) are uncited magic numbers (-6); `kx0_final = -2.65`, `m_eff = 0.0020`, `zeta = 0.080`, `tau_active = 0.18` (L377-380, inherited at L1000-1003) have no literature provenance and `nu = 0.28`, `c_stretch = 1.60` are chosen so alpha_c = 0.80 exactly (-5); `AP_REST_MV`/`AP_PEAK_MV` (L694-695) only colour the GIF (-1); the strip benchmark reports `ap_duration_half_amp_s = 0` because it has no probe nodes (L904) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py L214–L214: speedup_ratio_over_poroelastic hard-codes 56.0 ms <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/de27b685/2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py#L214-L214>",
        "2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py L373–L383: Unsourced motor constants tau_active 0.18 s, m_eff 0.0020, zeta 0.080, kx0_final -2.65 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/de27b685/2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py#L373-L383>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Forterre et al. (2005) Nature Doubly-Curved Shallow Shell Elastic Energy & Saddle-Node Cusp Catastrophe in Dionaea muscipula, coupled to a P1-FEM trigger-hair action potential and Ca2+ counting gate — Model fidelity to source: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Pass 2 shell model is intact: shallow-shell energy with Gauss stretching penalty (`gauss_stretching_energy` L231-244, `doubly_curved_shell_energy` L246-263), cusp fold metrics (L334-370) and RK45 coupled snap dynamics (`simulate_coupled_snap_dynamics` L373-451). Pass 3 adds a genuine, verified reduced electrophysiology layer: P1 FEM assembly (grad-grad stiffness + lumped mass, L778-796), IMEX FitzHugh-Nagumo solver with implicit diffusion via `splu` (L798-873), planar front speed within 2.5 % of the exact Nagumo formula (L725-731) and the two-touch Ca2+ gate on the rest curvature (L993-1067), backed by 5 Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys). Deductions: `relax_shell_equilibrium_2d` minimises `((kx+ky)/2)^2 - k_init^2)^2` (L300, L307) while the energy/gradient/dynamics use the Gauss product `(kx*ky - k_init^2)^2` — two different functionals, and its `barrier_energy` (L330) is the closed-form cusp expression, not derived from the minimisation (-6); the electrics are solved on a flat planform with no curvature feedback and FitzHugh-Nagumo stands in for the multi-channel Ca2+/Cl-/K+ AP (-5); the motor response is a scalar gate A(t) on a two-mode shell, not a turgor/curvature field (-4); the 0-D hair mechanics has no lever/podium geometry (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py L282–L333: relax_shell_equilibrium_2d minimises a mean-curvature functional ((kx+ky)/2)^2 at L300/L307 — inconsistent with the dynamics; barrier_energy at L330 is closed-form <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/de27b685/2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py#L282-L333>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-model-fidelity-4>,
