<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Forterre et al. (2005) Nature Doubly-Curved Shallow Shell Elastic Energy & Saddle-Node Cusp Catastrophe in Dionaea muscipula, coupled to a P1-FEM trigger-hair action potential and Ca2+ counting gate — MorphoEval overall 80.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py` (overall weighted score 80.4/100, down from 94.0 in v2). The Pass 2 remediation item is closed as an honest reduced model: a Boltzmann trigger-hair mechanotransducer initiates a P1 finite-element FitzHugh-Nagumo action potential on the lobe planform (planar front 9.55 vs exact Nagumo 9.80 cm/s, v ~ D^0.496, monotone h-convergence), a per-node Ca2+ counter implements the two-touch memory (analytic window 24.8 s bracketed by the sweep in (20, 25) s) and the activated-area fraction gates the Pass 2 shell solver (one touch -> no snap, two touches at 10 s -> snap with 354 ms latency). The score falls because the v2 credit for r = 1.0000 agreements was for model-vs-model comparisons (`*_obs` columns generated by the same analytics), the specimen \"reference values\" are self-recorded, the L-BFGS-B relaxation minimises a different functional from the dynamics, `--L`, `--h`, `--seed` are dead flags, the motor constants have no provenance, and the 8 new DOIs/literature values were recalled offline and are flagged `literature-approx` rather than digitised. Overall 80.4/100 (faithfulness 78.6, reproducibility 84.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit de27b685; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 78, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 80, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py at de27b685, image/png, 1861421 B, 2682×2407 px, artifact_sha256 435ac24cf8de9544178ac2abf5bf4f73f1d294d040244b2c5553a08c90ccd973 (sha256 435ac24cf8de9544178ac2abf5bf4f73f1d294d040244b2c5553a08c90ccd973), spec_fingerprint 58961469a41c2bee9701d676c847ef1e7a9835ee5baa9146d199bf480fec0179. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 58961469a41c2bee9701d676c847ef1e7a9835ee5baa9146d199bf480fec0179; artifact_sha256: 435ac24cf8de9544178ac2abf5bf4f73f1d294d040244b2c5553a08c90ccd973; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/dionaea_muscipula_trap_lobe_specimen.jpg=f2738290d66e4418..., datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/paper_citations.bib=b7c452b03e1fbba6..., datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/scout_manifest.json=572531a0986c798e..., datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/trigger_hair_ap_reference.json=76a6cb4ec8536b9a..., datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling_reference.json=593d9449e870fcf2...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Forterre et al. (2005): the Dionaea lobe is a doubly-curved shallow shell whose stretching-bending coupling alpha = L^4 kappa^2/h^2 produces a bistable snap-through (cusp catastrophe) once alpha exceeds a threshold; closure takes ~100 ms, far faster than the poroelastic limit; curvature-relief strip cutting abolishes snapping | Hedrich & Neher (2018), Böhm et al. (2016), Suda et al. (2020): two trigger-hair touches within ~30 s (two action potentials, a Ca2+ threshold) are required to close the trap; Hodick & Sievers (1988) / Volkov et al. (2008): the lobe AP propagates at cm/s speeds with ~1-2 s duration (values conflict between sources) | Scherzer et al. (2019), Procko et al. (2021): trigger hairs are micronewton mechanosensors with the stretch-activated channel FLYC1; reconstructed_in_script: 2D doubly-curved shallow shell energy U(kappa_x, kappa_y) with Gauss stretching penalty, L-BFGS-B equilibrium relaxation, cusp fold metrics and RK45 inertial + poroelastic snap dynamics across alpha in [0.2, 5.0] (Pass 2) | Boltzmann trigger-hair open probability -> receptor potential clamp on hair-footprint nodes -> P1-FEM IMEX FitzHugh-Nagumo action potential on a flat Delaunay lobe planform (2057 nodes), validated against the exact Nagumo front speed; per-node Ca2+ integrator with two-touch counting; lumped activated-area fraction A(t) gating the active rest curvature of the shell solver (Pass 3); transfer_boundary: The electrical problem is solved on a FLAT 2D planform mesh, not on the curved mid-surface, and the FEM does not see kappa(t); the motor response is a scalar gate A(t) on a two-mode shell, not a spatially resolved turgor field | AP_DIFFUSIVITY_CM2_S, AP_TAU_V_S, TRIGGER_HAIR_F_HALF_UN, CA_INCREMENT_PER_AP and CA_DECAY_TAU_S are model constants chosen so that the analytic speed, threshold and memory window land in the recalled literature ranges; agreement in measurements 14 and 17 is therefore parameter-driven, only the FEM-load elevation above the 0-D threshold (liminal ratio 1.55) is emergent | The `*_obs` columns of venus_flytrap_snap_buckling_reference.json are generated by the same model, so measurements 3-6 (r = 1.0000) are self-consistency checks, not comparisons with Forterre et al. (2005) data; does_not_claim: Hodgkin-Huxley-type Ca2+/Cl-/K+ channel kinetics, a trigger-hair lever/podium FEM, mechanical feedback from shell curvature onto the electrics, digitised Forterre (2005) Fig. 2-3 time series, or online-verified DOIs for the 8 electrophysiology references added in Pass 3." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py:1999-2001, 373-383, 214, 1317 — `--L`, `--h`, `--seed` are parsed but never used; `kx0_final = -2.65`, `m_eff = 0.0020`, `zeta = 0.080`, `tau_active = 0.18` have no literature provenance; `speedup_ratio_over_poroelastic` hard-codes 56.0 ms and the Stage II shading 0.21-0.30 s is hard-coded. Wire or remove the dead flags, source the motor constants (e.g. Sachse 2020 / Forterre 2005 Fig. 2) and compute the shaded interval from the simulated trajectory.",
        "remediation needed: 2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py:282-333 vs 246-281 — `relax_shell_equilibrium_2d` minimises ((kx+ky)/2)^2 - k_init^2)^2 (L300, L307) while `doubly_curved_shell_energy`/`_gradient` and the dynamics use the Gauss product (kx*ky - k_init^2)^2; its `barrier_energy` (L330) is the closed-form cusp formula. Make the relaxation minimise the same functional as the dynamics and derive the barrier from the saddle of that minimisation.",
        "remediation needed: 2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py:683-700, 925-931, 934, 1222 — `TRIGGER_HAIR_F_HALF_UN` = 2.9 µN, `AP_DIFFUSIVITY_CM2_S`, `AP_TAU_V_S`, `CA_INCREMENT_PER_AP`, `CA_DECAY_TAU_S` are tuned so that measurements 14 and 17 land on the recalled literature values; `evaluate_fem_mesh_convergence` holds `FEM_DT_S` fixed so the error plateaus at ~2.4 %; `--hair-force` never reaches `measure_morphoeval()`. Report tuned constants as calibration (not prediction) in the measurement notes, refine dt with h in the convergence study, and thread `--hair-force` into the measurements.",
        "remediation needed: 2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py:737-761, 798-873, 993-1067 — the electrics are solved on a flat Delaunay planform with FitzHugh-Nagumo kinetics and the motor response is a scalar activated-area gate A(t) on the two-mode shell. Solve the AP on the curved mid-surface (Laplace-Beltrami on the bilobed mesh of L1187-1214), replace FHN with a Hodgkin-Huxley-type Ca2+/Cl-/K+ channel model (Hedrich & Neher 2018), and let Ca2+ drive a spatially resolved turgor/rest-curvature field rather than a scalar gate.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/paper_citations.bib:48-141 and trigger_hair_ap_reference.json — all 8 new DOIs and every numeric literature value were recalled offline (`DOI unverified offline (Pass 3)`, `literature-approx`). Verify the DOIs online, digitise Hodick & Sievers (1988) / Hedrich & Neher (2018) AP speed and duration values, and resolve the Volkov (2008) m/s-ms vs Hodick & Sievers cm/s-s discrepancy.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling_reference.json `*_obs` columns and 2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py:1316, 1722-1791 — the alpha sweep, three-stage time series and developmental table are outputs of the same model (r = 1.0000 by construction) yet Panel C labels them \"Forterre et al. (2005) ref\", and specimen measurements 8-9 use self-recorded reference values 0.9745 / 0.3905. Replace with digitised Forterre (2005) Fig. 2-3 values (with provenance) and drop or relabel the self-referential specimen reference values." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.04e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Forterre et al. (2005) Nature Doubly-Curved Shallow Shell Elastic Energy & Saddle-Node Cusp Catastrophe in Dionaea muscipula, coupled to a P1-FEM trigger-hair action potential and Ca2+ counting gate — Parameter expressivity: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 sweeps remain (10 alpha values L452-540, 12-point kinematics L541-604, 5 developmental/ablation specimens L605-682). Pass 3 adds a diffusivity ablation sweep (`evaluate_diffusivity_scaling_sweep` L908-924, v ~ D^0.496), an h-refinement study (L925-931), a force bisection for the FEM initiation threshold (L969-992), an 8-interval two-touch memory sweep (L1074-1100) and three functional CLI flags `--hair-force`, `--touch-interval`, `--ap-diffusivity` (L1993-1995, dispatched at L2008-2017). Deductions: `--L`, `--h`, `--seed` (L1999-2001) are parsed but never used — there is no RNG and L/h are not passed to any solver (-10); `--hair-force` only affects the panels and GIF while `measure_morphoeval()` always uses 6.0 µN (L934, L1222) (-5); the mesh convergence study holds `FEM_DT_S` fixed so the error plateaus at ~2.4 % (-4); no sweep of hair position or footprint radius, although the footprint must exceed the 2D critical nucleus or nothing fires (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py L1993–L2001: --hair-force / --touch-interval / --ap-diffusivity functional; --L, --h, --seed parsed but unused <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/de27b685/2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py#L1993-L2001>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-parameter-expressivity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Forterre et al. (2005) Nature Doubly-Curved Shallow Shell Elastic Energy & Saddle-Node Cusp Catastrophe in Dionaea muscipula, coupled to a P1-FEM trigger-hair action potential and Ca2+ counting gate — Reproducibility package: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`self_test()` (L1881-1987) runs 12 suites in ~18 s: the 8 Pass 2 checks plus FEM accuracy/convergence/sqrt(D) scaling/K*1 = 0 & mass = area, lobe AP full activation and literature-range checks, two-touch counting incl. analytic bracket and lapsed memory, and bitwise determinism (two runs, atol = 0) plus A = 0 => kappa_x0 == k_init. All five dataset files are SHA-verified; the default run regenerates the PNG, both GIFs and re-runs the self-test (L2019-2023); the growth GIF regenerates bitwise identically to Pass 2. Deductions: dead `--L`/`--h`/`--seed` flags mislead users about what is reproducible under override (-4); default render takes ~45-49 s and the environment is not pinned by a lock file in this slot (-4); the self-test asserts model-internal consistency (sweep vs analytic window) where a literature check is implied (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py L1999–L2001: --L, --h, --seed parsed but unused <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/de27b685/2005-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling.py#L1999-L2001>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-repro-package-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Forterre et al. (2005) Nature Doubly-Curved Shallow Shell Elastic Energy & Saddle-Node Cusp Catastrophe in Dionaea muscipula, coupled to a P1-FEM trigger-hair action potential and Ca2+ counting gate — Source and data traceability: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Five dataset files are SHA-256-pinned and verified fail-closed at runtime (`EXPECTED_SHA256` L124-143, `verify_dataset_integrity` L155-167), including the new `trigger_hair_ap_reference.json`; `paper_citations.bib` carries 12 entries with DOIs and the module header lists all 12 sources (L1-76). The new JSON honestly tags every value with provenance and `doi_verified_offline: false`. Deductions: the 8 new DOIs and every new numeric literature value were recalled offline and are NOT verified (bib `note = {DOI unverified offline (Pass 3)}`) (-8); the Volkov 2008 (m/s, ms) vs Hodick & Sievers 1988 (cm/s, s) discrepancy on AP speed/duration is noted but unresolved (-4); the bib digest changed (f6ac2d52... -> b7c452b0...) so the v2 measurements' recorded digest is stale (-2); the `*_obs` reference columns in the Pass 2 JSON have no documented literature provenance (-6)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/paper_citations.bib L48–L141: 8 Pass 3 entries each with note = {DOI unverified offline (Pass 3)} <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/de27b685/datasets/venus_flytrap_snap_buckling/paper_citations.bib#L48-L141>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-source-traceability-2>,
