<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-forterre-venus-flytrap-snap-buckling-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Forterre et al. (2005) Nature Doubly-Curved Shallow Shell Elastic Energy & Saddle-Node Cusp Catastrophe in Dionaea muscipula, coupled to a P1-FEM trigger-hair action potential and Ca2+ counting gate — Morphological realism / specimen match: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The SHA-256-pinned CC BY-SA 2.5 Dionaea specimen is segmented into anthocyanin inner lobes, midrib hinge (x = 453 px) and 15 marginal cilia teeth (`segment_dionaea_trap_specimen` L1104-1185) and shown in Panel F; the new Panel G renders the FEM arrival-time map on the same ellipse planform as the bilobed mesh with the three hair positions, and the lobe conduction velocity 8.35 cm/s falls inside the recalled 6-20 cm/s range. Deductions: the 3D trap geometry of Panel A (`build_bilobed_trap_mesh` L1187-1214) is an illustrative parametrisation (0.42*kx+0.12, 0.22, 0.28, 0.18) not derived from the shell energy (-6); the specimen symmetry 0.9745 and cilia CV 0.3905 are compared with the script's own recorded outputs (L1776, L1786), so the specimen \"match\" is tautological (-6); hair positions `LOBE_TRIGGER_HAIRS_REL` (L700) and the 0.15 cm footprint (L687) are model placements, not measured from the specimen (-4); the planform mesh is flat and does not follow the segmented lobe contour (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
